  "system": "You are the test generator in Ledger. For one verified business rule of a legacy COBOL batch program you write test fixtures: complete, consistent sets of input records that exercise each branch of the rule and its boundaries. Every case is run through both the original COBOL program and a Python port, and their outputs are compared field by field, so a good case makes the rule's behaviour visible in the output files.\n\nGuidance:\n- One case per branch of the rule's When conditions, plus boundaries: values exactly at a limit, one cent over, a date equal to the limit and the day after, combinations of conditions where the rule says one result overrides another, zero and negative amounts where they matter.\n- Keep each case small (normally 1-4 records per file) but complete: every file the program reads gets consistent records with matching keys, unless the case is deliberately about a missing record.\n- Give values as strings: alphanumeric fields as text, numeric fields as plain decimal numbers such as \"1250.75\" or \"-40.00\" (no sign encoding, no padding). Omitted numeric fields default to 0 and omitted alphanumeric fields to spaces. Use the copybook field names exactly.\n- Call check_fixture on each fixture before you submit it and fix every error. Warnings may be intentional (for example a card that is deliberately missing).\n- Write 3 to 6 cases. In \"expectation\", say what the rule implies should happen; it is a note for reviewers, not the pass/fail oracle.",
  "messages": [
   {
    "role": "user",
    "content": "Program: CBACT04C. Input files and their record layouts:\n\nTCATBAL: CVTRA01Y TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  TRANCAT-ACCT-ID              9(11)\n  TRANCAT-TYPE-CD              X(2)\n  TRANCAT-CD                   9(4)\n  TRAN-CAT-BAL                 S9(9)V9(2)\n\nXREF: CVACT03Y CARD-XREF-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  XREF-CARD-NUM                X(16)\n  XREF-CUST-ID                 9(9)\n  XREF-ACCT-ID                 9(11)\n\nACCOUNT: CVACT01Y ACCOUNT-RECORD (300 bytes)\n  ACCT-ID                      9(11)\n  ACCT-ACTIVE-STATUS           X(1)\n  ACCT-CURR-BAL                S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CREDIT-LIMIT            S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CASH-CREDIT-LIMIT       S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-OPEN-DATE               X(10)\n  ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE          X(10)\n  ACCT-REISSUE-DATE            X(10)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT         S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT          S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-ADDR-ZIP                X(10)\n  ACCT-GROUP-ID                X(10)\n\nDISCGRP: CVTRA02Y DIS-GROUP-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  DIS-ACCT-GROUP-ID            X(10)\n  DIS-TRAN-TYPE-CD             X(2)\n  DIS-TRAN-CAT-CD              9(4)\n  DIS-INT-RATE                 S9(4)V9(2)\nThe program runs with job PARM '2022071800'. Account, cross-reference and disclosure group files are read by key, so every category balance's account needs ACCOUNT and XREF records.\n\nRule to test:\n{\n \"id\": \"BR-CBACT04C-001\",\n \"title\": \"Category balances are processed in account groups (control break on account ID)\",\n \"summary\": \"Category balance records are read one by one in key order. When the account ID changes, the account loaded before is written back with its interest (except on the very first record), the interest total is reset to zero, and the new account and its card cross-reference are read. Every record, including the first of a group, then goes on to rate lookup, and interest is only calculated when the rate is not zero.\",\n \"given\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"Category balance records are read one at a time, in key order, from the category balance file, which is indexed and read sequentially. The record key starts with the account ID, so all categories for one account come in together.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"TCATBAL-FILE\",\n    \"FD-TRAN-CAT-KEY\",\n    \"FD-TRANCAT-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"At program start the last-seen account number is spaces and the first-time flag is 'Y'.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM\",\n    \"WS-FIRST-TIME\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"Y\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"when\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"A category balance record is read and its account ID differs from the last-seen account number.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"END-OF-FILE\",\n    \"TRANCAT-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"N\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"then\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"If this is not the first account group, 1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT runs for the account loaded before: it adds the accumulated interest total to the account's current balance, sets the current-cycle credit and debit to 0, and rewrites the account record. On the first group the first-time flag is only set to 'N'.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-FIRST-TIME\",\n    \"WS-TOTAL-INT\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-BAL\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT\",\n    \"FD-ACCTFILE-REC\",\n    \"ACCOUNT-RECORD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"Y\",\n    \"N\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The interest total is reset to 0 and the last-seen account number is set to the new account ID.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-TOTAL-INT\",\n    \"WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM\",\n    \"TRANCAT-ACCT-ID\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"0\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The account record for the new account ID is read by key from the account file into ACCOUNT-RECORD.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"TRANCAT-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"FD-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"ACCOUNT-RECORD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The card cross-reference for the account is read through the account-ID alternate key. Its card number is the one later copied into the card number of each interest transaction.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"TRANCAT-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"FD-XREF-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"CARD-XREF-RECORD\",\n    \"XREF-CARD-NUM\",\n    \"TRAN-CARD-NUM\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"For every category balance record, whether or not the account changed, the rate lookup key is built from the account's group ID and the record's category code and type code, and the interest rate is looked up.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"ACCT-GROUP-ID\",\n    \"FD-DIS-ACCT-GROUP-ID\",\n    \"TRANCAT-CD\",\n    \"FD-DIS-TRAN-CAT-CD\",\n    \"TRANCAT-TYPE-CD\",\n    \"FD-DIS-TRAN-TYPE-CD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"Interest is calculated (and the fee step run) only when the interest rate found is not zero. Records with a zero rate add nothing to the account's interest total.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"DIS-INT-RATE\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"0\"\n   ]\n  }\n ]\n}"
   }
